7. Git and GitHub
7.1 What is Git?
Git is a version control system used to track changes in source code and manage different versions of a project.

Advantages of Git:

Tracks code changes.

Helps restore previous versions.

Supports teamwork.

Maintains project history.

7.2 What is GitHub?
GitHub is an online platform used to store, manage and share programming projects using Git.

Advantages of GitHub:

Stores project source code online.

Allows collaboration between developers.

Makes projects accessible to others.

Helps build a programming portfolio.

