8. Creating an Executable Python Application
Python programs can be converted into executable files using PyInstaller.

Installation:

pip install pyinstaller

Conversion:

pyinstaller --onefile program.py

This generates an executable file inside the dist folder (on Windows, the file generally has an .exe extension).

It allows users to run the application without manually executing the Python source file, although compatibility and required dependencies must be considered.

